      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-k/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Write W ∼N(µ, 42). (a) The lower-tail probability at 248 is 0.045. [M1] Convert 0.955 above to 1 −0.955 = 0.045 below: Thus (248 −µ)/4 = Φ−1(0.045). Therefore µ = 248 −4Φ−1(0.045) ≈254.7816, [A1] or 255 g . [M1] [A1] (b) Using µ = 255, [B1] [A1] P(250 &lt; W &lt; 256) = Φ(0.25) −Φ(−1.25) ≈0.4931 . [M1] [A1] (c) The probability is = Φ(0.25) −Φ(−1.75) P(248 &lt; W &lt; 256) ≈0.5820 . P(W &gt; 248) 1 −Φ(−1.75)\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-k/q7-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"[M1] Use conditional probability [B1] identify the overlap interval [A1] calculate the conditioning tail [A1] divide the two probabilities (d) The intersection for the preceding conditional event runs from 248 to 256. With the rounded mean, the standardised endpoints are (248 −255)/4 = −1.75 and (256 −255)/4 = 0.25. With p = 1 −Φ(−1.75), the count above 248 is B(10, p). [B1] The probability is ! 10 p6(1 −p)4 ≈0.000423 [A1] 6 to three significant figures: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 15 marks.</p>"
